where \([x]\) denotes the greatest integer function. If \(m\) and \(n\) respectively are the number of points in \((-2, 2)\) at which \(y = |f(x)|\) is not continuous and not differentiable, then \(m + n\) is equal to \(\underline{\hspace{1cm}}\) .
